{
  "name": "ears",
  "description": "ears is a high-level audio library for Rust that abstracts OpenAL and libsndfile to provide a simplified interface for spatialized sound playback and recording. It implements a dual-mode architecture consisting of memory-resident Sound buffers for low-latency effects and circular-buffered Music streams for large assets. The library handles listener kinematics, source-relative positioning, and metadata extraction, leveraging FFI bindings to manage low-level audio hardware and codec interactions.",
